          "source_quote": "ἀσύμφορόν ἐστι τῷ ἀνθρώπῳ τῷ τοιούτῳ",
          "english_quote": "it does not benefit such a person",
          "issue": "The English faithfully follows the selected working text, but note d does not disclose that its person-directed wording includes an editorial conjecture. The supplied apparatus identifies τῷ τοιούτῳ as Hilgenfeld’s conjecture, with versional support, and reports Athos τὸ τοιοῦτο instead. That alternative concerns the construction of the warning, separately from the disclosed repentance negation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the working English provisionally. Add a source-qualified disclosure that the printed τῷ τοιούτῳ is attributed to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture, supported by the listed versions, whereas the apparatus reports Athos τὸ τοιοῦτο. Explain the alternative construction without representing the conjectured Greek as preserved Athos wording. Any proposed alternative English requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐὰν δὲ ἐφ' ἑαυτῷ μείνῃ τις",
          "english_quote": "Remains unmarried expresses remaining by oneself in the widowed context.",
          "issue": "The contextual explanation is compatible with the working text, but it omits the supplied apparatus’s distinction between printed ἐφ’, attributed to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture with L₁/E support, and reported Athos ἐν, with L₂ marked doubtful. The note consequently explains the selected construction without identifying its editorial status or the stated alternative.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep the contextual rendering unless subsequent review finds a translation defect. Extend note f to identify the printed preposition as a reported editorial conjecture and distinguish the Athos and versional reports. Do not imply that the selected Greek construction is directly preserved in Athos.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Κύριε, ἐπεὶ ἅπαξ ἀνέχῃ μου, ἔτι μοι καὶ τοῦτο δήλωσον.",
          "english_quote": "The respectful Sir is a printed correction of Athos’s conjunction at the opening",
          "issue": "The alternative conjunction is disclosed, but “printed correction” does not accurately identify the supplied apparatus’s epistemic status: κύριε is explicitly attributed to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture with versional support. Calling it a correction can present the conjecture as an established repair of Athos rather than the selected editorial reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Describe “Sir” as following the working edition’s κύριε, which the supplied apparatus attributes to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture with L₁/L₂/E support; retain the already disclosed Athos καὶ alternative. No main-text replacement is required by the existence of that alternative.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
