          "source_quote": "ἀσύμφορόν ἐστι τῷ ἀνθρώπῳ τῷ τοιούτῳ",
          "english_quote": "it does not benefit them",
          "issue": "Independently assessed against the Greek, this preserves the working text’s person-directed warning. However, note d omits the supplied apparatus’s attribution of τῷ τοιούτῳ to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture and its report of Athos τὸ τοιοῦτο. Disclosure of the negation alternative does not disclose this separate editorial construction.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the simplified working rendering provisionally and add a concise disclosure distinguishing the conjectured printed construction, its reported versional support, and Athos τὸ τοιοῦτο. Submit any alternative English construction for fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐὰν δὲ ἐφ' ἑαυτῷ μείνῃ τις",
          "english_quote": "Remains unmarried expresses remaining by oneself in the widowed context.",
          "issue": "The note gives a source-compatible contextual interpretation but does not disclose that the supplied apparatus attributes printed ἐφ’ to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture, reports Athos ἐν, and distinguishes the supporting and doubtful versional evidence. The simplified edition inherits this disclosure defect independently of its otherwise compatible main-text wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add the reported editorial status and preposition alternative to note f, keeping Greek testimony, versional support, and conjecture distinct. Do not automatically change “stays unmarried” merely because an alternative preposition is reported.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Κύριε, ἐπεὶ ἅπαξ ἀνέχῃ μου, ἔτι μοι καὶ τοῦτο δήλωσον.",
          "english_quote": "The respectful Sir is a printed correction of Athos’s conjunction at the opening",
          "issue": "Although the note preserves the conjunction alternative, it labels the selected reading a “correction” rather than identifying the apparatus’s explicit attribution to Hilgenfeld’s conjecture. This blurs editorial reconstruction and reported preserved wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "State that “Sir” follows the working edition’s conjectural κύριε, attributed by the supplied apparatus to Hilgenfeld with L₁/L₂/E support, while Athos is reported to read καὶ. Retain the disclosed alternative opening and review any proposed replacement separately.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions cover all eleven paragraphs and preserve the selected source’s difficult repentance claims, negations, one-repentance teaching, remarriage permissions, and stated conditions. Reader-facing “servants” and contextual “repentance” comply with current policy. Revision is needed in the notes to distinguish additional reported editorial conjectures from preserved readings. The positive repentance reading should not be replaced merely because the negative alternative exists. This assessment uses the supplied working Greek and attributed reports; it does not authenticate unseen images or certify exhaustive collation."
